  "source_read_notes": [
    "DMG 77013 and 77015 distinguish the source meanings of couple and partner. DMG 77102 retains its estranged-couple example; sharing a dwelling alone does not establish one household.",
    "DMG 77100 and 77115 establish why household membership matters and identify possible members, including the temporary-living-apart qualification.",
    "DMG 77117 retains all listed exclusions and citations. DMG 77121 preserves the different both-partner permanent-care case; DMG 77122–77123 preserve all 52-week exception conditions and both examples. Further care-home/absence branches remain open, not inferred from these leads.",
    "DMG 77035 retains all dated savings/PSIC notes. DMG 77140 expressly distinguishes its household mixed-age definition from savings credit; DMG 77350 retains the 2016 SC restriction and its different definition. Relevant-date reconciliation remains unresolved.",
    "DMG 85016 retains both the ordinary partner-income attribution and the PSIC/household exception. No rule about all partner resources or a current award amount is inferred.",
    "DMG 85302 retains all three HB payment methods and the explicit claimant-landlord qualification. DMG 85230 retains the board-and-lodging/subtenant exclusions from its introductory disregard route; detailed treatment and reverse HB eligibility are not supplied.",
    "Source inconsistency retained: DMG 77117, point 1.2, cites DMG 77119, whereas the frozen DMG 77119 text addresses eight-week death-related absence and DMG 77122 expressly addresses the 52-week exception. Source locators are preserved without repairing the citation.",
    "Profiles express a conjunction of PC and the named topic. Generic partner/HB graph edges must not activate PC-only source routes for another benefit. Compiler/runtime traversal controls are required before adoption; profile activation alone is not sufficient proof."
  ]
}
